    info: 'Goddess Devi, worshipped at the Aattupurathu Devi Temple in Kayamkulam, Alappuzha, is a divine embodiment of feminine energy and power in Hinduism. Devotees revere Goddess Devi as the universal mother and source of creation, known by various names and forms across different regions and traditions. Devotees visit this temple to seek the blessings of the goddess for protection, prosperity, and fulfillment of their wishes. Festivals The Temple has a number of festivals. The important ones are : Punartham Maholsavam The Punartham Maholsavam, a significant festival, is celebrated at the Aattupurathu Devi Temple in Kayamkulam, Alappuzha, during the Malayalam month of Kumbham. This auspicious occasion is marked by vibrant rituals, cultural performances, and devotional offerings to the goddess. Devotees gather to seek the blessings of Goddess Devi for prosperity, well-being, and spiritual fulfillment during this festive period. Sarpabali Sarpabali, a distinctive ritual observed in temples devoted to snakes or serpents across Kerala, is believed to assist in alleviating various forms of Naga Doshas or afflictions. Typically conducted in the evening, this ritual is dedicated to the worship of Nagas and Ashta Nagas, the serpent deities. Devotees participate in Sarpabali seeking the blessings and protection of these divine entities, thereby seeking relief from afflictions associated with Naga Doshas. Contact Address: Aattupurathu DeviTemple, Kattachira, Pallikkal.P.O, Alappuzha, Kerala Phone Number:0479 2438498',
