    deity: '',
    deities: [],
    info: 'Velorvattom Sri Mahadeva Temple is believed to have been constructed in the 7th century by Azhvanchery Thamprakkal.According to legend, the installation of the idol of Lord Shiva was performed by sage Parasurama himself. This temple is unique as it features two Nalambalams (circumambulatory paths around the sanctum sanctorum) and two flag masts, distinguishing it from many other temples in Kerala. Festivals The Temple has a number of festivals. The important ones are : Thiru Ulsavam Thiru Ulsavam at the Velorvattom Sri Mahadeva Temple culminates in a grand celebration during the month of Kumbham. This festival, marked by vibrant rituals and fervent devotion, attracts scores of devotees who participate in the festivities with great enthusiasm. The temple resonates with the echoes of prayers and the vibrant atmosphere of cultural celebrations during this auspicious occasion. Ramayana Maasa Acharanam During the Ramayana Maasa Acharanam observed in the month of Karkkidakam, the Velorvattom Sri Mahadeva Temple conducts various sacred rituals to commemorate the epic of Ramayana. These rituals include Ganapathi Homam, Mrityunjaya Homam, and Ksheeradhara, among others, invoking blessings for protection, prosperity, and spiritual well-being. Devotees participate in these ceremonies with devotion, seeking divine grace and auspiciousness during this holy month dedicated to the revered Ramayana scripture. Contact Address: Velorvattom Sri Mahadeva Temple, Cherthala Rd, Velorvattom, Cherthala, Alappuzha, Kerala 688524 Phone Number: 0478 281 3466',
